hildren":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables manual pagination. If this option is set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the table will not automatically paginate rows using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPaginatedRowModel()"},{"type":"text","value":" and instead will expect you to manually paginate the rows before passing them to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side pagination and aggregation."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onpaginationchange","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onPaginationChange?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional onPaginationChange: OnChangeFn<PaginationState>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L32","children":[{"type":"text","value":"features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:32"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Called with an updater when pagination state changes. Pair this with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.pagination"},{"type":"text","value":" when using external state; external atoms can own the\nslice without this callback."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"pagecount","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pageCount?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional pageCount: number;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L36","children":[{"type":"text","value":"features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:36"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageCount"},{"type":"text","value":" value to the table if you know it (Or supply a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowCount"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageCount"},{"type":"text","value":" will be calculated). If you do not know how many pages there are, you can set this to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-1"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rowcount","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rowCount?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional rowCount: number;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L40","children":[{"type":"text","value":"features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:40"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowCount"},{"type":"text","value":" value to the table if you know it. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageCount"},{"type":"text","value":" can be calculated from this value and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageSize"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"interface-tableoptions-rowpagination","text":"Interface: TableOptions_RowPagination","level":1},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"autoresetpageindex","text":"autoResetPageIndex?","level":3},{"id":"manualpagination","text":"manualPagination?","level":3},{"id":"onpaginationchange","text":"onPaginationChange?","level":3},{"id":"pagecount","text":"pageCount?","level":3},{"id":"rowcount","text":"rowCount?","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Interface: TableOptions\\_RowPagination\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:18](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L18)\n\n## Properties\n\n### autoResetPageIndex?\n\n```ts\noptional autoResetPageIndex: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:22](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L22)\n\nIf set to `true`, pagination will be reset to the first page when page-altering state changes e.g. `data` is updated, filters change, grouping changes, etc.\n\n***\n\n### manualPagination?\n\n```ts\noptional manualPagination: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:26](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L26)\n\nEnables manual pagination. If this option is set to `true`, the table will not automatically paginate rows using `getPaginatedRowModel()` and instead will expect you to manually paginate the rows before passing them to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side pagination and aggregation.\n\n***\n\n### onPaginationChange?\n\n```ts\noptional onPaginationChange: OnChangeFn<PaginationState>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:32](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L32)\n\nCalled with an updater when pagination state changes. Pair this with\n`state.pagination` when using external state; external atoms can own the\nslice without this callback.\n\n***\n\n### pageCount?\n\n```ts\noptional pageCount: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:36](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L36)\n\nWhen manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total `pageCount` value to the table if you know it (Or supply a `rowCount` and `pageCount` will be calculated). If you do not know how many pages there are, you can set this to `-1`.\n\n***\n\n### rowCount?\n\n```ts\noptional rowCount: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:40](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L40)\n\nWhen manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total `rowCount` value to the table if you know it. The `pageCount` can be calculated from this value and the `pageSize`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: TableOptions_RowPagination\ntitle: TableOptions_RowPagination\n---\n\n# Interface: TableOptions\\_RowPagination\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:18](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L18)\n\n## Properties\n\n### autoResetPageIndex?\n\n```ts\noptional autoResetPageIndex: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:22](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L22)\n\nIf set to `true`, pagination will be reset to the first page when page-altering state changes e.g. `data` is updated, filters change, grouping changes, etc.\n\n***\n\n### manualPagination?\n\n```ts\noptional manualPagination: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:26](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L26)\n\nEnables manual pagination. If this option is set to `true`, the table will not automatically paginate rows using `getPaginatedRowModel()` and instead will expect you to manually paginate the rows before passing them to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side pagination and aggregation.\n\n***\n\n### onPaginationChange?\n\n```ts\noptional onPaginationChange: OnChangeFn<PaginationState>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:32](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L32)\n\nCalled with an updater when pagination state changes. Pair this with\n`state.pagination` when using external state; external atoms can own the\nslice without this callback.\n\n***\n\n### pageCount?\n\n```ts\noptional pageCount: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:36](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L36)\n\nWhen manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total `pageCount` value to the table if you know it (Or supply a `rowCount` and `pageCount` will be calculated). If you do not know how many pages there are, you can set this to `-1`.\n\n***\n\n### rowCount?\n\n```ts\noptional rowCount: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts:40](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/row-pagination/rowPaginationFeature.types.ts#L40)\n\nWhen manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total `rowCount` value to the table if you know it. The `pageCount` can be calculated from this value and the `pageSize`.\n"}
